29|/// A monotonic counter identifying a specific version of game state.
30|///
31|/// The initial revision is `0`. Each successful command creates the next revision (`1`, `2`, …).
32|/// The type is a transparent `u64` newtype so it prevents accidental mixing with unrelated
33|/// counters. Serde uses a canonical decimal string so all 64 bits survive JSON and JavaScript
34|/// round trips without exceeding JavaScript's safe-integer range (`2^53 - 1`); `u64` serialized
35|/// as a JSON number would lose precision in JS and via `wasm-bindgen`.
36|#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, Eq, Hash, Ord, PartialEq, PartialOrd)]
37|#[repr(transparent)]
38|pub struct GameRevision(u64);
